{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore","id":473754,"title":"Is Primal Urge worth getting anymore","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-08T20:17:25-07:00","id":473754,"title":"Is Primal Urge worth getting anymore","content":"DaveB said somewhere that Spirit Rank and Primal Urge were not supposed to be D&amp;D-line challenge equalizing stats. I got to thinking after that about what Primal Urge really means now in WtF2E.<br /> <br /> -It lets you store more Essence. Up to Primal Urge 5, that's just one more Essence holding spot per dot of PU, though.<br /> -It lets you use Essence faster. This is handy for the first couple of tiers, but there's not all that much you'd need to spend Essence on all at once anymore. If you're still at starter Harmony, you might need it to shift reflexively, plus to have the round's healing be lethal damage, plus maybe a Gift or two. Influence powers cost a comparative ton of Essence at one Essence per dot of the power you're using. Even so, I imagine you'd be really hard pressed to need as many as five Essence in a turn ever what with the lack of &quot;spend Essence to add two dice to your strength pool&quot; type mechanics that littered 1E.<br /> -It makes you better at Clashes of Wills. So does the Renown in question, though PU can go higher than Renowns.<br /> -It lets you regenerate health faster. But not until PU 4, and then again at PU 6.<br /> -It lets you sniff out spirits' infuence. But you subtract their Resistence from the roll, so...<br /> -It makes you generally better at tracking stuff once you hit PU 4.<br /> -It makes your Lunacy harder to resist, again at PU 4.<br /> -It makes food harder to digest.<br /> -It makes your Death Rage last longer. This could be good if you're Raging alongside rival werewolves with lower PU. It will be very bad in almost all other circumstances.<br /> -It makes you need to hunt more often lest you start to bleed Essence and Break Towards Flesh.<br /> <br /> I feel like there's probably a lot of stuff I forgot (oh! like general resistance to supernatural powers). I guess there are a lot of small benefits to Primal Urge. It felt like there were far more instances of &quot;Skill/Attribute + Primal Urge&quot; in the first edition games and far less now.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else have thoughts on this? Benefits or drawbacks I missed? Reasonable analyses of why, between all of those things, Primal Urge is or is not a good investment over Skills or Renown or Gift Facets or Merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:45:30-07:00","id":473797,"title":"","content":"It also adds to Toxin resistance, resisting mind control during Death Rage, a few of the senses get bonuses. Hearing is spectacular in the country, 'When accessing her wolf senses, an Uratha can hear from a distance of one mile (or two kilometers) per dot of Primal Urge.' Your Hishu and Dalu form abilities are enhanced by it, and there's a minor hack offered on page 286. That was more to just add to your list.<br /> <br /> So far I think there's two things I'd change if I could hijack the book on the way to wherever. Skin Thief's human-skin ability is too limited, and Primal Urge ramps up really late. I'd have 4B regeneration at 7 and 8, moving all the healing up one so you had your first 2B at 3 Primal Urge, and move the Basu-Im, Lunacy Penalty and Tracking Bonus down with it. It seems like a really weird change from 1 to 2 Primal Urge where the only real difference is in essence and diet. Though I guess it now means you can regenerate and use gifts, so with mid range Primal Urge you won't be tempted to go into Gauru for a quick full heal. I'm not much of a mechanics guy, obviously you can buy into a new gift or get two new facets or a renown and there's probably some sort of cost efficiency effectiveness concept in the RPG community I'm unaware of but I think that won't always make sense for the character. Which might be a cop out but even in my game I can see a lot of gifts that I'd really like, but wouldn't really fit the character yet.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you seem to be right, it doesn't look like there's gifts and stuff that work off of Primal Urge but the tracking, Lunacy, senses and other things are good changes. Someone was theorizing on another board the other day about how Pure would be different, and one thing they suggested was that they might have Wolf Gifts that have prerequisites, like Primal Urge for Predator Kings or Low Harmony for Fire-Touched. Forsaken could get them, of course, but they would be considered more standard for the Pure. I don't know what they're going to do with Primal Urge but other than my previous paragraph I don't really have a complaint about it. It doesn't affect every power you have but Renown does and so now Renown is important. I imagine Primal Urge will get more depth and things to take advantage of if we get more books, but it looks like it's more about the core of your werewolf, no gifts or rites or tribal concerns, just the base hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-08-2015, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:00:17-07:00","id":473807,"title":"","content":"A lot of Werewolf Merits have Primal Urge prerequisites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:02:54-07:00","id":473809,"title":"","content":"Being able to just drop a bunch of those reflexive gifts at once alone says yes for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:08:08-07:00","id":473814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=473807#post473807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of Werewolf Merits have Primal Urge prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know about a <i>lot</i>, so far it seems to be just Instinctive Defense and Favored Form, but the latter does have an increasing prerequisite of 'Primal Urge at the Merit rating +1.' So you'd need 6 Primal Urge to get all the merits and make one form significantly enhanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:46:24-07:00","id":473849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=473814#post473814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know about a <i>lot</i>, so far it seems to be just Instinctive Defense and Favored Form, but the latter does have an increasing prerequisite of 'Primal Urge at the Merit rating +1.' So you'd need 6 Primal Urge to get all the merits and make one form significantly enhanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it just felt like a lot because I REALLY LIKE both of those Merits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:52:33-07:00","id":473856,"title":"","content":"I'd like Favored Form but I don't think I'd be able to narrow the choice of form down to one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2015, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T04:50:15-07:00","id":474093,"title":"","content":"You do start cap-breaking just as the extra essence per turn starts being superfluous, so in that sense at least you trade one useful advantage for another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:03:06-07:00","id":474123,"title":"","content":"That extra mile of hearing thing is neat.<br /> <br /> I like the concept behind Favored Form a lot, but the two restrictions on it seem pretty odd and were a bit of a turn off. The first is the Primal Purge of 2-6 you mentioned, which when coupled with my doubts above made it seem like a pretty steep price for the Merit. The other is that Hishu is off the list. Now, sure, it's the least wolfish, but all five forms are supposed to be natural for the Uratha, not just the hairy ones. The reason I would want it is that I play an Ithaeur Bone Shadow, and a lot of the special abilities they get use Manipulation as their main attribute. But Manipulation can't be helped by Favored Form because all the more lupine forms take a penalty to it. It's a cool concept, but the restrictions make it not for me.<br /> <br /> As to reflexive gifts, and such, a lot of them are up for a whole scene. That one that mitigates a bunch of damage isn't, but I can't recall any other counter examples at the moment. I'm sure there are more and I'd love to have them called out. My point behind bringing it up, though, is that you only need to put of the lot of them once. That being the case, having a Dedicated Locus you tend to could fill the gap if you really need to fire them all at once. Sure, each dot is one Essence per day, but unless you're in a several scenes long conflict, that will be a minor setback most of the time. It'll be a pretty major setback when it is drained and you do need it, though, especially if the thing you didn't have an extra Essence to spend for was regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:16:09-07:00","id":474130,"title":"","content":"I think the reason you can't take hishu as a favoured form is that you're kind of assumed to favour it by default. <br /> <br /> Which brings up interesting questions if one decides to hack-in wolf born werewolves, but that's another matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:23:14-07:00","id":474134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474123#post474123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That extra mile of hearing thing is neat.<br /> <br /> I like the concept behind Favored Form a lot, but the two restrictions on it seem pretty odd and were a bit of a turn off. The first is the Primal Purge of 2-6 you mentioned, which when coupled with my doubts above made it seem like a pretty steep price for the Merit. The other is that Hishu is off the list. Now, sure, it's the least wolfish, but all five forms are supposed to be natural for the Uratha, not just the hairy ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bugs me a bit, too. Especially since it isn't the only merit that has the restriction. Both Fortified Form and Living Weapon are only applicable in forms other than Hishu. Granted, a human with strangely thick skin and stronger bones and sharp teeth that could rend through armor sort of dampens the forms purpose, to hide among humanity. But I don't like it as a restriction. I could see Predator Kings, for instance, with those two merits so that their human form was more 'bestial,' and not as toothless as the rest of humanity. Or an Ivory Claw whose favored human form is a manipulator to the utmost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:39:31-07:00","id":474137,"title":"","content":"See, I'm not so sure a predator king would go that route. I'd much more expect one to basically use dalu as hishu and ignore their original form entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:59:53-07:00","id":474160,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think all of them would do it, but I'm sure some would, were it possible. Especially if the Lodge of Vermin's Shadow is still around. What better way to prove you're a true predator than turning your 'hiding' form into a lethal weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2015, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T07:46:41-07:00","id":474297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=473797#post473797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there's a minor hack offered on page 286. ...<br /> I'm not much of a mechanics guy, obviously you can buy into a new gift or get two new facets or a renown and there's probably some sort of cost efficiency effectiveness concept in the RPG community I'm unaware of but I think that won't always make sense for the character. Which might be a cop out but even in my game I can see a lot of gifts that I'd really like, but wouldn't really fit the character yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read that hack for the first time. I really really like it. There have been a ton of things that I've run across where I've thought it through and come to &quot;but the negative modifiers on that would make it almost impossible to ever do...&quot; I'm a little confused by the second paragraph of it, though. It says &quot;roll to resist Kuruth&quot;. What with Wasu-Im, rolling to resist Kuruth seems to have been dropped from the game. I guess this is an issue of &quot;you're calling on your wolfy core in such a way that might be akin to taking Gauru outside of combat if you can't will yourself to keep it together.&quot; So one roll of Resolve + Composure? When, if ever do you erase the marks above your Primal Urge track? Is the use that puts you straight into the Death Rage marked down? Is the one that puts you right into Death Rage your PU+1th attempt or your 11th attempt?<br /> I realize it's called out as a hack in the book, but it's one of few things making me think Primal Urge is important, so I'd like to see it work.<br /> <br /> As to the mechanical, cost/benefit side of things - my brain kinda runs in &quot;how does this system work&quot; circles all the time anyway. In the case of playing Werewolf, though, my group only meets once a month. That means that 1 Experience = 1 month of real life time in my world. Thus, it is a fairly precious comodity and the ability to put it to good use is imoprtant to me. Given the long gaps between games, there may well be times when we skip ahead and say &quot;everyone did some stuff and got 10xp for it!&quot; I might grab a dot of Primal Urge during those, but sitting around for nigh-on half a year for it still sounds iffy.<br /> <br /> That hack does make it tempting, though...<br /> <br /> Oh! one other main point on the cost/benefit side of things: Renown is pretty much super-powered nowadays. They grant Gifts, give extra dice to those Gifts, and determine your effective Rank against Spirits, which eventually means you naturally cause aggravated damage to the lesser ones (or, with that Purity/Warding Facet, the big ones). And so long as your Storyteller is cooperative enough to put you in situations where you could do something awesome enough to warrant the new dot, it's easier to come (cheaper) than Primal Urge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":".  added the last paragraph 04-09-2015, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T07:57:03-07:00","id":474305,"title":"","content":"If I were to use the hack, gut instinct, I would say it resets whenever you hit Basu-im (because the wolf has had a proper run around and isn't banging the door of it's cage any more) and maybe also slowly ticks down over time. Say, one mark a day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T08:05:24-07:00","id":474310,"title":"","content":"Wasu-Im and Basu-Im are both considered part of Kuruth, so you could probably still roll for it.<br /> <br /> I would have you only erase the marks when you've gone Kuruth because of it, so after you've filled up. So at Primal Urge 1 you'd get 2 uses out of it. One puts the mark up, the next one 'acts' with full marks. I'd rule it that way, at least.<br /> <br /> Addendum: I like Elfive's 'ticking down by day' idea.<br /> <br /> Yes, I could see the issue with that. I've had some bad luck with aspirations and things, so I haven't gotten much in the way of Experiences, but we generally play about once a week or so. Still, Primal Urge is considerably cheaper now. Depending on your game, if you're running it or it has a limited duration, so this wouldn't be too game-breaking, you might offer a Primal Urge for every successful, but momentous, Siskur-Dah. I wouldn't use that in my own games, which tend to be sandboxes, or a more long-running story unless I had a series of 9 previously determined 'prey' that would lead to the big finale, but if you had a shorter game it might be a nice way to do it, reflecting a werewolf's progress through the Siskur-Dah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2015, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T08:21:50-07:00","id":474321,"title":"","content":"I really like all those ideas recently expressed. Both the reset - at - rage and the ticking down bit seem like good systems. Maybe the ticking down one would have some sort of rest addendum, kinda like how you get a point of Willpower back if you have a good night's rest. Maybe you could pick one of those dots instead of a Willpower when you would otherwise get a Willpower back. I hesitate on this one for the full-Willpower-refreshes, but as one of them involves raging and the other involves really asserting your not-so-beasty-side, those seem to make sense, too.<br /> <br /> I also really like the momentous Siskur-Dah success building your Primal Urge idea. I get how people with a more open world and more constant play would want to keep with the 5xp = Primal Urge thing, but for other situations that sounds great to me. Now it wouldn't be for those &quot;we must hunt so lets go rout some spirit&quot; hunts, but maybe for the big ones that defend your territory from a major and strong threat, those could do it. I like it.<br /> Thanks nofather. And Elfive. And the other people who contributed overnight that I can't see right now because I'm looking at page two and your post is on page 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:39:04-07:00","id":474406,"title":"","content":"I think it would be nice to have an optional hack for Primal Beats, like the one from Vampire for Blood Beats. Thing is, I don't know what kind of things would offer Primal Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:44:11-07:00","id":474410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474406#post474406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be nice to have an optional hack for Primal Beats, like the one from Vampire for Blood Beats. Thing is, I don't know what kind of things would offer Primal Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of a few things. Siskur-Dah in excess of your 'minimum necessary sacred hunting' based on your Primal Urge level, for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:48:10-07:00","id":474417,"title":"","content":"Primal Beats does make sense, too. There was Arcane Experience in Mage, and given how central the concept was to DaveB's Imperial Mysteries book, I assume it will take the form of Arcane Beats in the new edition.<br /> What sorts of things generate Blood Beats in Vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:26:43-07:00","id":474469,"title":"","content":"<b>Primal Beats</b><br /> <br /> - You go on a Hunt in excess of your minimum requirement.<br /> - You enter Basu-Im.<br /> - You use your Hunter's Aspect on a mortal.<br /> - You successfully use a form to its stated purpose.<br /> - You exemplify your Auspice without flaring Renown.<br /> - You exemplify your Tribe.<br /> <br /> There's probably more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:33:01-07:00","id":474472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474417#post474417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Beats does make sense, too. There was Arcane Experience in Mage, and given how central the concept was to DaveB's Imperial Mysteries book, I assume it will take the form of Arcane Beats in the new edition.<br /> What sorts of things generate Blood Beats in Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dramatic Failures on Discipline rolls.<br /> Exceptional Success on Discipline rolls<br /> Embracing<br /> Ghouling<br /> Creating revenants<br /> Exsanguinating a victim<br /> Frenzy or riding the wave<br /> Spending your last Vitae<br /> Drinking beyond capacity - I like this one<br /> Joining a bloodline<br /> Gaining a Discipline dot<br /> Rolling for Detachment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:43:40-07:00","id":474483,"title":"","content":"While a lot of your points are valid, I am genuinely confused by the title. Is Primal Urge worth getting <i>anymore</i>? Was it worth getting before? It was prohibitively expensive in 1e and past primal urge 3 (which you'd almost have to get at character creation) there was very little incentive to pay 32 experience or more for a single dot in primal urge. Now there are a lot more reasons that primal urge is relevant than Signs of the Moon and it's just flat out more affordable. Now there are also some drawbacks, but those make sense and are fun to roleplay if you're into that sort of thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:51:18-07:00","id":474488,"title":"","content":"Is Detachment akin to Harmony? Or is it Integrity upside-down? Is the expectation that you'll be rolling for it anywhere near as often as Harmony?<br /> <br /> Gebbethine's examples seem like good ones, and very in-keeping with werewolf-y themes. Some of the Vampire ones don't seem like they would translate well, though some do. <br /> The dramatic failures and exceptional successes and super-skill dot bits seem fine, though the three about spreading vampiness just don't have any correlative WtF concepts (Lunacy, maybe?). <br /> Exsanguinating seems like it would map to Agg-Flakes, which has enough carrots attached to it already in my opinion. <br /> Frenzy maps to Kuruth, which was suggested above, too.<br /> Do spending your last Vitae and your last Essence have other similar effects? Like does it make you lapse into a coma like spirits who spend their last Essence? I know nothing running out of Vitae and can't remember what happens to Werewolves.<br /> Drinking beyond capacity... maybe this one would be more like Agg-Flakes and the other one would be more like hunting more than necessary...<br /> Bloodlines are functionally similar to Lodges, right?<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, though, any exceptional success on Siskur-Dah grants a regular Beat.<br /> And are the Dramatic Failure Blood Beats in addition to the Beat you normally get for taking a dramatic failure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:01:25-07:00","id":474496,"title":"","content":"I think they are as they are specific on disciplines. That said, you could make more wolf blooded so long as they fail a lunacy degeneration check. Dramatically. Hell one of the tells involves getting bitten by a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm assuming they do not take the place of the one dramatic failure beat as they apply specifically to generating experience for blood potency purchases. It's a way to avoid blowing your main exp on blood potency purchases. page 276 of blood and smoke 2nd. <br /> <br /> Actually answers one of my questions about using different methods to generate beastial nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 04-09-2015, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:24:44-07:00","id":474540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474483#post474483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a lot of your points are valid, I am genuinely confused by the title. Is Primal Urge worth getting <i>anymore</i>? Was it worth getting before? It was prohibitively expensive in 1e and past primal urge 3 (which you'd almost have to get at character creation) there was very little incentive to pay 32 experience or more for a single dot in primal urge. Now there are a lot more reasons that primal urge is relevant than Signs of the Moon and it's just flat out more affordable. Now there are also some drawbacks, but those make sense and are fun to roleplay if you're into that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really play that much 1E stuff. I read through it, and boggled at the general idea of xp costs increasing with dots on things that went up to 10 (did anyone, anywhere, ever put their morality stat up even as high as 8?). I never actually faced the prospect of spending 32xp on my fourth dot of PU, though. I did look through Vampire 1E and saw single Devotions costing that much and more and thought &quot;who would ever do that&quot;.<br /> <br /> The reason I put an &quot;anymore&quot; on the title, though, was that, in reading the 1E books, it seemed like the Power Stat (Primal Urge, Blood Potentcy, Gnosis to a much greater extent, etc.) were everywhere. My recollection of those books was that you could hardly go a few pages without some dice pool or other having the Power Stat tagged on. That felt much less true in Werewolf 2E than I remember it being in 1E. Sure, it was super expensive, but then everything was. The fourth dot in your Renown tied to your Auspice or Tribe was 24XP, for example.<br /> <br /> While it may seem a lot more possible to get it now (a phenomenon that doesn't strike as close to home for me as it does for many), it also looks a lot less useful than it seemed to be. Hence &quot;anymore&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:29:44-07:00","id":474546,"title":"","content":"Due to how healing works, and the obvious advantages and lack of disadvantages, compared to first edition, second edition Primal Urge is worth getting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474488#post474488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Detachment akin to Harmony? Or is it Integrity upside-down? Is the expectation that you'll be rolling for it anywhere near as often as Harmony?<br /> <br /> Do spending your last Vitae and your last Essence have other similar effects? Like does it make you lapse into a coma like spirits who spend their last Essence? I know nothing running out of Vitae and can't remember what happens to Werewolves.<br /> Bloodlines are functionally similar to Lodges, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Detatchment is losing a dot of Humanity. Humanity for vampires doesn't go up and down like Harmony, you have to buy it up. In this way it's morelike Integrity. It's been my experience that you won't roll as often as Harmony, but experience varies.<br /> <br /> Using all your Vitae or Essence doesn't seem to have an effect, on its own, other than not having power for your abilities. A vampire empty of Vitae may be more susceptible to frenzy, as they could have a penalty for it. Also, they spend a Vitae to wake up each night, so without that Vitae if you do go to 'sleep' during the day or get knocked into torpor you won't be able to wake up without help.<br /> <br /> And yes, although there's a significant difference in the fluff for it, generally being 'inherited,' they are functionally similar to lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:33:00-07:00","id":474549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474483#post474483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a lot of your points are valid, I am genuinely confused by the title. Is Primal Urge worth getting <i>anymore</i>? Was it worth getting before? It was prohibitively expensive in 1e and past primal urge 3 (which you'd almost have to get at character creation) there was very little incentive to pay 32 experience or more for a single dot in primal urge. Now there are a lot more reasons that primal urge is relevant than Signs of the Moon and it's just flat out more affordable. Now there are also some drawbacks, but those make sense and are fun to roleplay if you're into that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In our Long Running San Francisco Campaign, we had One Werewolf (Bone Shadow Itheaur) at Primal Urge 5, One Werewolf (Hunter in Darkness Cahalith) at Primal Urge 4, One (Iron Master Irraka ) at 3 Primal Urge and the Cub (Hunter Irraka) at PU 1. None of these were purchased ahead of time (No dots assigned at Character Creation). Everyone, except the Cub, sought out Primal Urge over the course of the campaign, thought the Iron Master resisted it a lot, due to his social focus (not that the PU penalties ever really impacted his social role (or rolls) much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> There are reasons even in 1st Edition, and they are no less fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:36:05-07:00","id":474572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474540#post474540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't really play that much 1E stuff. I read through it, and boggled at the general idea of xp costs increasing with dots on things that went up to 10 (did anyone, anywhere, ever put their morality stat up even as high as 8?). I never actually faced the prospect of spending 32xp on my fourth dot of PU, though. I did look through Vampire 1E and saw single Devotions costing that much and more and thought &quot;who would ever do that&quot;.<br /> <br /> The reason I put an &quot;anymore&quot; on the title, though, was that, in reading the 1E books, it seemed like the Power Stat (Primal Urge, Blood Potentcy, Gnosis to a much greater extent, etc.) were everywhere. My recollection of those books was that you could hardly go a few pages without some dice pool or other having the Power Stat tagged on. That felt much less true in Werewolf 2E than I remember it being in 1E. Sure, it was super expensive, but then everything was. The fourth dot in your Renown tied to your Auspice or Tribe was 24XP, for example.<br /> <br /> While it may seem a lot more possible to get it now (a phenomenon that doesn't strike as close to home for me as it does for many), it also looks a lot less useful than it seemed to be. Hence &quot;anymore&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our Bone Shadow Itheaur kept her Harmony hovering around 9-10 (it wavered occasionally, but she would work to regain it). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:47:07-07:00","id":474623,"title":"","content":"Well I mean in a long running game, eventually you are going to get your primal urge up due to stat caps and just realizing all your other priorities, but I mean in the short term there was never much reason to raise primal urge, especially considering the social penalty which honestly was pretty huge. I'm glad that's gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as reasons to raise it now, I think the fact that it's the resistance trait for all supernatural powers is still a pretty big deal, especially as a campaign goes on. And I think it appears just as much if not more often than in 1E. Clash of Wills makes it especially important when dealing with other splats contesting your powers. The increase on healing is also really nice.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T06:42:18-07:00","id":475754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474123#post474123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the concept behind Favored Form a lot, but the two restrictions on it seem pretty odd and were a bit of a turn off. The first is the Primal Purge of 2-6 you mentioned, which when coupled with my doubts above made it seem like a pretty steep price for the Merit. The other is that Hishu is off the list. Now, sure, it's the least wolfish, but all five forms are supposed to be natural for the Uratha, not just the hairy ones. The reason I would want it is that I play an Ithaeur Bone Shadow, and a lot of the special abilities they get use Manipulation as their main attribute. But Manipulation can't be helped by Favored Form because all the more lupine forms take a penalty to it. It's a cool concept, but the restrictions make it not for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are not new Hishu advantage - &quot;Sheep's Clothing&quot; - giving you Primal Urge penalty to tracking you supernatural nature? So higher you are in Primal Urge, harder it is to point out you as this big and scary werewolf tearing humans and monsters apart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-10-2015, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T07:58:08-07:00","id":475829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=475754#post475754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are not new Hishu advantage - &amp;quot;Sheep's Clothing&amp;quot; - giving you Primal Urge penalty to tracking you supernatural nature? So higher you are in Primal Urge, harder it is to point out you as this big and scary werewolf tearing humans and monsters apart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's really handy. The issue I was addressing was that as a ritualist character, who needs Manipulation to pull stuff off and thus would favor Hishu form (the only form that doesn't penalize the stat), you can't make use of the Favored Form Merit. It seemed odd to me.<br /> <br /> Good point though about Sheep's Clothing working better with higher Primal Urge. Badass Motherfucker for Dalu does, too, which is nice for people that don't have a lot of Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:05:29-07:00","id":475839,"title":"","content":"If you want a specialized form for doing rituals, you could take Father's Form and put your Favored Form bonuses there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:16:49-07:00","id":475845,"title":"","content":"Rituals can use pretty much any dice pool you want now. In fact, of the example rites given a grand total of <i>one</i> uses manipulation. It's just not a werewolf-y attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:52:01-07:00","id":475889,"title":"","content":"It seems like Iron Masters and Ivory Claws might get a lot of use out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:08:51-07:00","id":475914,"title":"","content":"Ressonance Shaper (p107), Shadow Masquerade (p116), and Heart of Water (p123) all take Manipulation + Occult. Sure, Rites proper can take any dice pool, but with three major immutable pools requiring that combo, my character is already specialized in it and thus it becomes a good pool for Rites.<br /> <br /> The Father's Form idea is a pretty good one, though I'm unclear how being in that Gauru form affects social stuff. Normally, Gauru just fail all social and mental rolls. Favored Form's boost-an-attribute dots specifically call out Gauru as the form with a penalized Manipulation, even though it's the only non-Hishu form without Manipulation specifically called out as penalized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:13:56-07:00","id":475923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=475914#post475914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ressonance Shaper (p107), Shadow Masquerade (p116), and Heart of Water (p123) all take Manipulation + Occult. Sure, Rites proper can take any dice pool, but with three major immutable pools requiring that combo, my character is already specialized in it and thus it becomes a good pool for Rites.<br /> <br /> The Father's Form idea is a pretty good one, though I'm unclear how being in that Gauru form affects social stuff. Normally, Gauru just fail all social and mental rolls. Favored Form's boost-an-attribute dots specifically call out Gauru as the form with a penalized Manipulation, even though it's the only non-Hishu form without Manipulation specifically called out as penalized.</div> </div> </div> </div>They normally auto-fail due to Rage. Father's Form prevents that, allowing you to craft it into a ritual specific form using Favored Form. Garou form being a ritual form is actually one of the things discussed in the essay about Father's Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:26:53-07:00","id":475931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=475923#post475923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They normally auto-fail due to Rage. Father's Form prevents that, allowing you to craft it into a ritual specific form using Favored Form. Garou form being a ritual form is actually one of the things discussed in the essay about Father's Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but as also pointed out, rituals don't need to involve mental or social activity (Attributes). It is a pretty interesting idea. If my group played more often, I'd think about going that route.<br /> <br /> Makes me giggle a bit thinking of Gauru as the best form for Social Manipulation, though... It makes a lot more sense when those interactions are with spirits, but still. <br /> One of the things I fell it love with about Werewolf when I first played it was how fluid and utilitarian the forms are. I need to make this jump, so I need more Dex, so I shuold jump as an Urshul. I really need to hold down my beefy packmate before he does something stupid, so I need to be stronger so I should grab him with Gauru and hope to God my Willpower of 6 holds out for two rolls. Adding the &quot;I'm gonna have to lie to this guy and I want to have the best chance of him believing me so... Gauru!&quot; scenario is humerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:41:54-07:00","id":475942,"title":"","content":"That's why its a Breaking Point towards flesh. That tactic, while valid by my reading, is very routed in rational thought, while Gauru's purpose is to be the opposite. It works, but it pulls you away from your spiritual side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:50:01-07:00","id":475951,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't be a breaking point if, after lying to the guy, I hit him. <br /> The thing that made it seem funny, more than anything, was the idea of being mid conversation with someone and having them suddenly turn into a big wolf for no discernable reason. It's like Pinocchio's nose on the most intense steroids ever cooked up. Plus causing Lunacy while attempting to get away with lying is highly counterproductive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:01:46-07:00","id":475963,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it works well for boosting Manipulation dice pools, not so much for actual social interaction, except with other werewolves and wolf-blooded. Which is appropriate, I think. Definitely a funny mental image though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:07:03-07:00","id":475980,"title":"","content":"&quot;Are you wearing contacts, Dave? I could have sworn you had blue eyes.&quot;<br /> &quot;Uh, [grows 3 feet taller, 600 pounds heavier, sprouts fur and claws] no. My eyes have always been this color...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:33:43-07:00","id":476204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/473754-is-primal-urge-worth-getting-anymore?p=474472#post474472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dramatic Failures on Discipline rolls.<br /> Exceptional Success on Discipline rolls<br /> Embracing<br /> Ghouling<br /> Creating revenants<br /> Exsanguinating a victim<br /> Frenzy or riding the wave<br /> Spending your last Vitae<br /> Drinking beyond capacity - I like this one<br /> Joining a bloodline<br /> Gaining a Discipline dot<br /> Rolling for Detachment</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting back on the Primal Beats idea, it just occurred to me that with the Harmony system being so different than any of the other Integrity systems, maybe Primal Beats were dropped for a good reason: there's a whole category of thing Werewolves never have to spend Experiences on.<br /> How many of the above Blood Beat signifiers also cause rolls for Detachment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:04:15-07:00","id":476219,"title":"","content":"Embracing doesn't have a detachment roll, it always has a Humanity cost of one dot.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, Ghouling and Riding the Wave at Humanity 8, Creating Revenants at 2, Exsanguinating a victim always causes it but at different levels depending on the reason behind it. Rolling for Detachment, surprisingly, never causes another roll for detachment on its own.<br /> <br /> A vampire can choose to take a bane for some of these, meaning they no longer cause detachment checks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:13:31-07:00","id":476226,"title":"","content":"Hmm, that's a lot of them... I wonder if this is why there aren't Primal Beats.<br /> <br /> I still like the idea of Primal Beats, though. And the PU goes up after a major Siskur-Dah is successful. I'll be bringing them up with my ST.<br /> <br /> (on a side note, someone was talking about the God Machine and called it the GM. I couldn't help but wonder if the acronym usually used for 'dude running the game' for other RPGs was intentionally overlayed into WoD as 'the insane and tyranical overlord-mind-thing that wants nothing but obedience and order'. O.O )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:42:16-07:00","id":476255,"title":"","content":"It might be because Humanity is a one way street. A loss is a loss, it must be bought back, and at 0 you're relegated to a draugr, forever lost to your monstrous desires. If you ran breaking points as Primal Beats, you could just go down and up and down and up and down and up until you had all you wanted and you're right back where you started at Harmony 7, no worse for the wear.<br /> <br /> Primal Urge seems like the Father Wolf side of things. That, the wolf gifts. Those are part of being the hunter. P86, 'It reflects her progress through the <i>Siskur-Dah</i>, following the footsteps of <i>Urfarah </i>to become a bodhisattva predator, a true inheritor of Mother Wolf's legacy.'<br /> <br /> Harmony, breaking points, auspices, that's the forever shifting influence of Luna. Just like your flesh shifts from form to form, the moon from phase to phase, your Harmony moves and flows.<br /> <br /> Primal beats, as an aspect in advancement of Primal Urge, shouldn't really have much to do with Harmony, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-10-2015, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T06:44:25-07:00","id":476871,"title":"","content":"Right. That was kindof my point: it seems like a lot of the Blood Beats come when you're facing negative Experiences on your Humanity. Being as the remedy for Harmony loss is to act more human and roll for it, balancing it with Experience gains for some other thing is less of a thing.<br /> <br /> The only place in Werewolf where you lose something you need to spend Experiences to gain back is the loss of the Totem Merit when you trespass the pack ban or otherwise piss your Totem off. Being as pissing spirits off was one of Father Wolf's main jobs, those two things seem like fine candidates for Primal Beats, along with the other things suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}